This directory is empty on purpose, and it must not be deleted.

gt/intel_rps.c includes the Ironlake power controller's header by a path that
climbs out of the driver tree:

	#include "../../../platform/x86/intel_ips.h"

We stage only drivers/gpu/drm/i915, so that header is not in the source tree,
and imported source is never edited to change the spelling of an include. The
substitute lives at ../../../platform/x86/intel_ips.h relative to THIS
directory, and the Makefile puts this directory on the include path
(I915_IMPORT_CFLAGS) so the climb lands on it.

The climb is resolved by the filesystem, not lexically by the preprocessor:
clang concatenates the -I directory with the quoted path and asks the kernel to
open it, so every component of this path has to exist as a real directory. Git
does not track empty directories, so without a file here the path disappears on
a fresh clone and `make B1NIX_I915=1` fails with

	fatal error: '../../../platform/x86/intel_ips.h' file not found

on a checkout where the header is plainly present. This file is that anchor.
